1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:00:55,458 --> 00:00:56,667
Mr. Jang.

7
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:01,833
You know everything, don't you?

8
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,583
Are you drunk?

9
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:27,792
Is that why you're acting like this?

10
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:32,167
Yeah.

11
00:01:37,458 --> 00:01:39,292
Aren't you mad at me?

12
00:01:43,625 --> 00:01:45,375
Why would I be mad?

13
00:01:49,917 --> 00:01:51,542
Because of this?

14
00:01:57,958 --> 00:02:00,000
Why would I be mad over this?

15
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:06,000
I'd rather you just lash out at me.

16
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:21,667
You don't mean that much to me.

17
00:02:31,333 --> 00:02:34,375
You got it now, you can leave. I'm tired.

18
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,167
I went here so we can talk.

19
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:00,458
I have nothing to say to you.

20
00:03:02,458 --> 00:03:04,167
You figured it out, didn't you?

21
00:03:05,125 --> 00:03:07,708
That the person you've
been chatting with all this time

22
00:03:09,792 --> 00:03:11,292
is me.

23
00:03:17,208 --> 00:03:20,125
If you're mad, get mad at me.
If you have questions, just ask.

24
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:22,125
Just say something. Anything.

25
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,625
I can take it.

26
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:26,510
Is there something you
want to hear from me?

27
00:03:27,583 --> 00:03:29,125
Fine.

28
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:38,667
I did it on purpose.

29
00:03:44,917 --> 00:03:47,875
I knew it was you from the very beginning.

30
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:52,005
And you still have nothing
to talk to me about?

31
00:03:56,417 --> 00:03:58,000
Was it fun?

32
00:04:01,917 --> 00:04:05,000
Constantly messing with someone
whose life is dull and boring...

33
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,167
Did that amuse you?

34
00:04:17,417 --> 00:04:19,125
So, did you[r heart] waver?

35
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:34,542
Yeah.

36
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,400
I wavered.

37
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:40,309
Every single day, I wondered
what kind of person you were.

38
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:41,750
Are you satisfied now?

39
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:46,208
Just leave.

40
00:04:46,917 --> 00:04:48,583
I told you what you wanted to hear.

41
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:52,250
Then why did you do that earlier?

42
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,958
That kiss just now...

43
00:04:55,792 --> 00:04:56,583
What did it mean?

44
00:04:56,708 --> 00:04:58,833
Let's just sleep together
once and end this.

45
00:05:01,375 --> 00:05:04,000
Isn't that why you approached
me in the first place?

46
00:05:04,792 --> 00:05:07,250
Sleeping with me should satisfy you, right?

47
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:13,083
And I won't have to
keep doing this with you.

48
00:05:28,625 --> 00:05:34,500
Do you hate... talking to me that much?

49
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:39,125
What's left to say?

50
00:05:48,042 --> 00:05:49,542
Alright.

51
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:53,083
Let's do it.

52
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:05,667
You have to look at me properly.

53
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:11,658
Didn't you say we'd end it
all after we slept together?

54
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:51,875
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 7)

55
00:08:22,667 --> 00:08:24,500
We aren't done yet.

56
00:08:27,667 --> 00:08:29,542
Because from start to finish today,

57
00:08:31,333 --> 00:08:33,833
you didn't look at me
properly, not even once.

58
00:08:42,083 --> 00:08:44,125
So this is all your fault.

59
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:51,792
(So this is all your fault.)

60
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:00,750
(Delete Amuna)

61
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:09,083
(Confirm)

62
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,042
May I ask where you spent the night?

63
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:07,292
At a friend's place.

64
00:10:07,417 --> 00:10:08,792
Which friend?

65
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:15,250
Did my dad tell you to ask?

66
00:10:15,375 --> 00:10:17,458
It'd better not be Kim Ji Tae.

67
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,833
Get ready for school.

68
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:40,792
I'm seriously curious
about Jang Gi-woo's type.

69
00:10:40,917 --> 00:10:42,018
It's gotta be someone
from our school, right?

70
00:10:42,042 --> 00:10:43,375
Could it be someone in our class?

71
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:45,875
Hyeon-jong, you're getting
all this on camera, right?

72
00:10:57,292 --> 00:11:00,458
There's a cash prize for guessing
who Jang Gi-woo was chatting with.

73
00:11:00,583 --> 00:11:01,583
How much?

74
00:11:01,667 --> 00:11:03,333
More than what I make on TikTok?

75
00:11:03,792 --> 00:11:05,351
Your TikTok is flopping
because you're in it.

76
00:11:05,375 --> 00:11:06,458
Yeah, right.

77
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,917
What did you just say?

78
00:11:10,458 --> 00:11:14,083
We're talking about Mr. Jang
Gi-woo getting exposed.

79
00:11:14,917 --> 00:11:16,833
Why, do you want a shot
at the prize money too?

80
00:11:19,542 --> 00:11:21,809
(Gi-woo, wanna meet up? I have something
for you.) (Wanna come over to my place?)

81
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:24,433
(I had fun today. Thanks for the
coffee.) (Sure. Are you asleep?)

82
00:11:41,625 --> 00:11:42,875
Lee Hyeon-jae!

83
00:11:47,958 --> 00:11:49,375
Lee Hyeon-jae.

84
00:11:54,625 --> 00:11:56,000
Go back to your seat.

85
00:12:06,542 --> 00:12:09,083
The guy chatting with Jang
Gi-woo is definitely Lee Hyeon-jae.

86
00:12:09,208 --> 00:12:10,375
It's 100% him.

87
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,809
Because they have
that kind of relationship,

88
00:12:11,833 --> 00:12:14,553
he covered for Lee Hyeon-jae
even after he got caught selling pills.

89
00:12:46,958 --> 00:12:48,083
Hyeon-jae.

90
00:12:50,042 --> 00:12:51,250
Hyeon-jae!

91
00:12:52,708 --> 00:12:56,583
Do you have any of those pills left?

92
00:12:57,667 --> 00:12:59,458
Are you still selling them?

93
00:12:59,583 --> 00:13:00,917
What did you say?

94
00:13:03,042 --> 00:13:06,583
Those pills. Are you still selling them?

95
00:13:08,292 --> 00:13:10,333
I don't do that.

96
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:12,292
Choi Young-moon told me everything.

97
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:14,000
He said you used to sell them.

98
00:13:16,042 --> 00:13:18,875
If you have any left, can I just get one?

99
00:13:19,583 --> 00:13:23,167
I can't pay you right away,

100
00:13:23,917 --> 00:13:24,792
but I'll find a way to get the money.

101
00:13:24,917 --> 00:13:26,250
I told you, I'm not selling.

102
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:32,208
I heard you're the one who
was chatting with Mr. Jang.

103
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:34,167
I'll tell everyone about it.

104
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,375
Just give me one.

105
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,042
I get so anxious without
it. I can't focus at all.

106
00:13:44,167 --> 00:13:47,000
I owe Kim Ji Tae a ton of money,
so I have nowhere else to get them.

107
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:05,375
Hey.

108
00:14:10,708 --> 00:14:12,083
Take two at once.

109
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:15,627
For someone like you, one
won't be strong enough.

110
00:14:16,958 --> 00:14:18,167
Thank you.

111
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:20,470
If anything goes wrong, I'll take the fall.

112
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:26,083
Just tell them I sold them to you.

113
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,250
Take two at once.

114
00:14:39,083 --> 00:14:41,083
Do you know who the other person is?

115
00:14:41,542 --> 00:14:43,583
We'll have the posts
taken down, so don't worry.

116
00:14:45,583 --> 00:14:47,375
Where did this leak from?

117
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,208
That social media site the students use?

118
00:14:51,208 --> 00:14:53,333
You don't know who it was, right?

119
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:56,917
No, I don't.

120
00:14:58,083 --> 00:15:00,125
Then keep playing dumb.

121
00:15:01,542 --> 00:15:03,542
Just like before.

122
00:15:04,083 --> 00:15:06,542
Play dumb and keep your mouth shut.

123
00:15:09,458 --> 00:15:11,750
The AC in my classroom is broken.

124
00:15:11,875 --> 00:15:14,208
Class 3 is the coolest, right?

125
00:15:29,667 --> 00:15:33,458
Mr. Jang, do you know
who you were chatting with?

126
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,167
Seems like they're the one who leaked it.

127
00:15:36,917 --> 00:15:39,583
You actually know who it is,
don't you? You're just holding back.

128
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:41,167
Are you trying to protect them?

129
00:15:41,708 --> 00:15:43,292
No.

130
00:15:43,417 --> 00:15:46,125
I don't know who it is. I have no clue.

131
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,625
You must be really
disappointed in the students.

132
00:15:51,917 --> 00:15:56,750
Don't let it get to you, or
they'll use it against you.

133
00:15:57,125 --> 00:16:00,667
I told you not to get too
emotionally invested in them.

134
00:16:06,917 --> 00:16:09,208
Take your time eating.

135
00:16:09,583 --> 00:16:11,792
We're all done.

136
00:16:12,583 --> 00:16:13,667
Everyone's finished, right?

137
00:16:13,792 --> 00:16:15,125
Yeah, looks like it.

138
00:16:15,625 --> 00:16:16,792
Let's go.

139
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,458
(Lee Hyeon-jae)

140
00:17:28,042 --> 00:17:29,750
I have something for you.

141
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:45,042
Having feelings for someone
can actually be a mistake.

142
00:17:47,958 --> 00:17:49,500
I finally understand that now.

143
00:18:12,125 --> 00:18:13,485
Make sure you wear it from now on.

144
00:18:20,583 --> 00:18:23,125
Those photos going around right now,

145
00:18:24,292 --> 00:18:25,500
and the chat logs...

146
00:18:29,667 --> 00:18:31,375
That wasn't you.

147
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,000
Never admit to it.

148
00:18:37,167 --> 00:18:38,417
Why?

149
00:18:43,208 --> 00:18:45,333
That's the only way to
keep this from blowing up.

150
00:18:48,917 --> 00:18:50,458
Because you're the chairman's son.

151
00:19:00,208 --> 00:19:02,125
(English: 1:10 PM - 2:20 PM) (70 minutes)

152
00:19:12,708 --> 00:19:14,333
(English Section)

153
00:19:32,958 --> 00:19:34,083
What did you just take?

154
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:38,500
Headache medicine.

155
00:20:10,583 --> 00:20:11,667
Hey... Hyeon-jong!

156
00:20:11,792 --> 00:20:13,042
What's wrong with you?

157
00:20:14,333 --> 00:20:16,833
Keep your eyes on your
test. Don't get distracted.

158
00:20:19,708 --> 00:20:20,958
Hyeon-jong.

159
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,792
Hyeon-jong!

160
00:20:22,917 --> 00:20:23,958
What's wrong with you?

161
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:26,400
Goodness.

162
00:20:26,417 --> 00:20:28,458
(Lee Hyeon-jae) Hey! Hyeon-jong!

163
00:20:35,167 --> 00:20:36,458
Mr. Jang.

164
00:20:36,667 --> 00:20:39,167
Hyeon-jong's mother is here.

165
00:20:39,292 --> 00:20:41,542
She's in your classroom. Hurry over there.

166
00:20:53,917 --> 00:20:55,250
(Lee Hyeon-jae)

167
00:21:02,708 --> 00:21:04,375
Who is Lee Hyeon-jae?

168
00:21:11,208 --> 00:21:12,375
That's me.

169
00:21:19,542 --> 00:21:22,875
Miss, let's step outside to talk.

170
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:25,917
Sixth period is about to
start. Please understand.

171
00:21:27,167 --> 00:21:28,875
I am not walking out of here alone!

172
00:21:29,583 --> 00:21:32,333
My son already blew one of his exams,

173
00:21:33,708 --> 00:21:35,708
and this kid just gets
to sit here and finish his?

174
00:21:36,917 --> 00:21:38,583
Tell me the truth.

175
00:21:38,708 --> 00:21:42,125
You gave this to my son, didn't you?

176
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:43,833
Didn't you?!

177
00:21:43,958 --> 00:21:45,750
He asked for it, so I gave it to him.

178
00:21:47,250 --> 00:21:48,542
Did you hear that?

179
00:21:48,667 --> 00:21:49,458
Let's step outside and
discuss this properly.

180
00:21:49,583 --> 00:21:53,167
How are we supposed to discuss
anything without him here?!

181
00:21:53,292 --> 00:21:55,792
I'll go with you.

182
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:57,875
Lee Hyeon-jae.

183
00:22:03,792 --> 00:22:05,292
I'll take responsibility.

184
00:22:19,333 --> 00:22:21,958
I am not letting this slide!

185
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:25,042
Do you have any idea how
crucial the sixth mock exam is?!

186
00:22:25,167 --> 00:22:27,184
Do you know how many
subjects he has ruined by now!?

187
00:22:27,208 --> 00:22:29,875
He asked to buy them first.
That's why I gave them to him.

188
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,250
Look at this kid's attitude!

189
00:22:31,375 --> 00:22:34,333
He's acting like he did nothing wrong!

190
00:22:34,458 --> 00:22:37,542
Are you just going to
let him get away with this?

191
00:22:47,333 --> 00:22:51,250
I apologize for keeping you waiting.

192
00:22:54,042 --> 00:22:55,500
You're here?

193
00:22:57,625 --> 00:22:58,792
Dad...

194
00:22:59,708 --> 00:23:03,375
What? He's the chairman's son?

195
00:23:08,042 --> 00:23:11,625
The school will handle this matter
thoroughly, so please don't worry.

196
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,792
First, we'll have a proper
talk with Hyeon-jong.

197
00:23:14,917 --> 00:23:17,167
But he's your son, Mr. Chairman!

198
00:23:17,292 --> 00:23:19,125
How am I supposed to trust you?

199
00:23:22,208 --> 00:23:23,292
Mr. Jang Gi-woo.

200
00:23:24,667 --> 00:23:27,958
Please accompany his mother and
hear Hyeon-jong's side of the story.

201
00:23:29,750 --> 00:23:30,917
Yes, sir.

202
00:23:31,250 --> 00:23:34,000
Hey, I'm not letting this go.

203
00:23:34,667 --> 00:23:38,083
I'm calling the police,
so brace yourselves.

204
00:23:55,667 --> 00:23:57,333
You fucking brat.

205
00:23:57,458 --> 00:23:59,058
What the hell do you think you're doing?

206
00:24:00,417 --> 00:24:02,417
I wanted to humiliate you.

207
00:24:03,583 --> 00:24:04,208
Why, you little...

208
00:24:04,333 --> 00:24:06,750
I bought those pills from
Kim Ji Tae for 20 million won

209
00:24:07,458 --> 00:24:08,875
to sell them at school.

210
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,167
Your secretary wired the
money. Go ahead and check.

211
00:24:11,292 --> 00:24:12,458
Lee Hyeon-jae!

212
00:24:14,292 --> 00:24:15,625
Just expel me.

213
00:24:16,375 --> 00:24:18,895
You were keeping quiet until
now. Why are you acting out again?

214
00:24:26,750 --> 00:24:28,990
Because I finally have
something I can't afford to lose.

215
00:24:29,583 --> 00:24:31,250
Are you really going to stay silent?

216
00:24:31,375 --> 00:24:33,833
He claims you asked him for the pills.

217
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:36,625
Is that true?

218
00:24:39,792 --> 00:24:43,167
Hyeon-jong, it's okay. Tell the truth.

219
00:24:46,417 --> 00:24:48,167
I asked him for them.

220
00:24:50,250 --> 00:24:52,792
Choi Young-moon's grades
shot up out of nowhere.

221
00:24:53,750 --> 00:24:56,417
I got jealous, so I stole
his pills and took them.

222
00:24:57,750 --> 00:25:00,708
When I couldn't get more, I borrowed
money from Kim Ji Tae to buy them.

223
00:25:04,292 --> 00:25:06,542
Will this go on my permanent record?

224
00:25:06,667 --> 00:25:07,875
No, right?

225
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,625
Mr. Jang, I'm technically
the victim here, right?

226
00:25:16,417 --> 00:25:20,042
Good job today, everyone. You can
check the answer keys when you get home.

227
00:25:25,625 --> 00:25:27,809
Those whose names I call,
report to the faculty office.

228
00:25:27,833 --> 00:25:30,917
Choi Young-moon, Park Min-ha, Seo Do-jun,

229
00:25:31,708 --> 00:25:33,000
and Kim Jeong-ha.

230
00:25:34,667 --> 00:25:35,917
Class dismissed.

231
00:25:36,042 --> 00:25:37,458
Why me?

232
00:25:43,542 --> 00:25:44,875
Shit!

233
00:25:50,833 --> 00:25:52,042
Kim Jeong-ha.

234
00:25:53,750 --> 00:25:55,750
I'll wait for you so we
can walk home together.

235
00:25:58,083 --> 00:25:59,125
Just go ahead without me.

236
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:19,542
You're the last one.

237
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,917
How is your grandmother?
Was she discharged?

238
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:26,375
I heard it's just the two of you.

239
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,833
She was transferred to a nursing home.

240
00:26:30,875 --> 00:26:32,167
That's a relief.

241
00:26:35,333 --> 00:26:37,833
That's the reason I started
working for Kim Ji Tae.

242
00:26:39,792 --> 00:26:43,125
Lim Hyeon-jong borrowing
money from Kim Ji Tae for the pills...

243
00:26:43,875 --> 00:26:45,167
I knew all about it.

244
00:26:46,458 --> 00:26:48,458
I even knew he stole his mom's bag.

245
00:26:53,583 --> 00:26:55,583
Didn't I tell you to call
me if anything happened?

246
00:26:57,375 --> 00:26:59,833
Back then, I told you to
call me if you were in trouble.

247
00:27:01,500 --> 00:27:03,833
Things got this bad, and
you didn't even call me once.

248
00:27:05,167 --> 00:27:06,417
Even if I had told you,

249
00:27:11,208 --> 00:27:12,625
what difference would it have made?

250
00:27:14,625 --> 00:27:15,958
Mr. Jang.

251
00:27:17,792 --> 00:27:19,792
Are you like this with all your students?

252
00:27:22,833 --> 00:27:27,833
Are you like this with all your students?

253
00:27:33,167 --> 00:27:34,750
What do you mean by that?

254
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,708
You always act like you're
willing to help with anything,

255
00:27:41,625 --> 00:27:43,745
when in reality, there's
nothing you can actually do.

256
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:51,500
And that's the worst part.

257
00:27:53,850 --> 00:27:56,000
Acting like you'll listen to everything.

258
00:28:08,333 --> 00:28:09,958
Come on, let's go to my place.

259
00:28:10,083 --> 00:28:11,292
Why would I go there?

260
00:28:12,125 --> 00:28:13,292
Let's have dinner together.

261
00:28:20,042 --> 00:28:22,292
You're not going to do
anything reckless anymore, right?

262
00:28:24,542 --> 00:28:27,333
Who are you to decide
what's reckless or not?

263
00:28:27,792 --> 00:28:29,125
Who do you think you are?

264
00:28:32,458 --> 00:28:34,000
Fine, let's get this straight then.

265
00:28:34,875 --> 00:28:36,375
What am I?

266
00:28:40,875 --> 00:28:43,208
What the hell am I to you?

267
00:28:43,750 --> 00:28:45,167
Say it yourself.

268
00:28:47,250 --> 00:28:48,958
Or should I go first?

269
00:28:49,667 --> 00:28:52,917
Yeah, I've been avoiding you.

270
00:28:53,458 --> 00:28:56,458
Because I felt like it was all my
fault that your wrist got ruined.

271
00:28:58,208 --> 00:29:00,000
That's why I kept avoiding you.

272
00:29:00,125 --> 00:29:01,708
What, my reputation at school?

273
00:29:02,583 --> 00:29:04,792
I never once cared about that.

274
00:29:05,917 --> 00:29:08,250
Your grandma told me something back then.

275
00:29:08,792 --> 00:29:10,708
She told me not to get too close to you.

276
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:13,875
She said unlike me, you didn't
grow up in a happy, wealthy family,

277
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,458
so I shouldn't give you false hope.

278
00:29:22,875 --> 00:29:24,315
Why are you telling me all this now?

279
00:29:24,375 --> 00:29:25,958
Because things ended up like this!

280
00:29:27,833 --> 00:29:29,750
Because you ended up like this!

281
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:36,260
Then you shouldn't have pushed
me to the point where I had to say it!

282
00:29:43,917 --> 00:29:45,292
Can't we just...

283
00:29:46,667 --> 00:29:48,708
go back to how we used to be?

284
00:29:49,917 --> 00:29:51,500
Can't we just do that?

285
00:29:56,583 --> 00:29:58,042
I like you.

286
00:30:02,833 --> 00:30:05,553
You have no idea what it feels
like for me to have feelings for you.

287
00:30:06,708 --> 00:30:08,468
And you probably don't
want to know, either.

288
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,875
I can't go back to how we used to be.

289
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:18,250
So just leave me alone.

290
00:30:39,750 --> 00:30:40,870
I'm heading out for the day.

291
00:30:40,917 --> 00:30:42,042
Okay, have a good night.

292
00:30:44,708 --> 00:30:49,375
Mr. Jang, have you seen Hyeon-jae?

293
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:53,042
He probably went home. Look at the time.

294
00:30:55,542 --> 00:30:56,875
Aren't you leaving yet?

295
00:30:57,417 --> 00:30:58,833
I'm going to stay a little longer.

296
00:31:00,583 --> 00:31:01,792
Have a good night.

297
00:31:12,667 --> 00:31:14,292
(Promotional message)

298
00:31:48,542 --> 00:31:50,083
We aren't done yet.

299
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:01,125
This is all your fault.

300
00:33:15,042 --> 00:33:16,458
I knew you'd come find me.

301
00:33:18,250 --> 00:33:19,583
Mr. Jang.
